-- title:
--   Unit indicator coefficients for probability parameters
-- statement:
--   For a vertex $v$ of an arbitrary type, its unit indicator is the closed-unit-interval-valued function
--
--   $$\mathbf1_v(w)=\begin{cases}1,&w=v,\\0,&w\ne v.\end{cases}$$
--
--   These coefficients select one vertex's probability mass when inserted into a weighted-coordinate parameter. This elementary definition is the selected interface from the module on uniform affine support charts; quantitative continuity theorems are provided separately.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Continuous graph homomorphisms of higher dimensional abelian group actions, arXiv:2609.39824v1 (2026), Section(s) 4, 7.1; https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.39824v1. This item is auxiliary infrastructure of the accompanying formalization; its implementation definitions are not asserted to be separately numbered in the paper. Original Lean module AbelianTargets/UniformAffineSupportCharts.lean, selected declaration lines 21; SHA-256 97ba5022a771ec9935b2ee2f163000db7fb6b64a8f3cd4d14e74cbce48b288a7. Selected spans are from the final generated manifest. The original source snapshot is local; no public repository URL or commit was available.

